@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "March 24, 2025 - The Purge 2 in TMUF";
}

<h1>March 24, 2025 - The Purge 2 in TMUF</h1>
<p><small>Last updated: <time datetime="2025-03-25">March 25, 2025</time></small></p>
<p>
    A noticable change has been made again in the Trackmania United Forever leaderboards on March 24, 2025, which fully applied ingame on March 25.
    In response to the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ox6zF48YXkQ">Exposing Trackmania's Biggest Con-Man...</a> investigation initiated by Arkes,
    Nadeo has acknowledged the alt account problem in Trackmania United Forever, and removed all of the records driven on proved alt accounts,
    most notably those belonging to riolu. The records were removed during March 24, but ingame, they have been publically updated
    on the next day (with the exception of opponent skillpoints, which updated immediately, as it uses a different kind of request).
    It was possible to extract the leaderboard data from 25rd and the day before using some simple reverse engineering techniques.
</p>
<p>
    In comparison from the Purge 1 from July 23, 2021, this one is focused entirely on alt accounts, and not any other cheating methods.
    Many of these accounts had records removed that weren't ever proved to be cheated via an external software.
</p>
<p>
    This leaderboard change was announced by <a href="https://x.com/Hylis1/status/1904239315787677978">Hylis on X</a> on March 24, 19:30 CET.
</p>

